7. Meanwhile, if the petitioner, named above, is arrested, he shall be released on interim pre-arrest bail, in connection with the above noted case, on furnishing bail bond of Rs.30,000/- (Rupees Thirty Thousand only) with two local sureties of like amount to the satisfaction of the arresting authority, subject, of course, to the following conditions:
(i) That the petitioner shall appear before the Investigating Officer within 10 days from today and on such other dates as may be necessary;
(ii) That the petitioner will deposit his passport, if it was been issued to him, before the I.O.
(ii) That the petitioner shall not hamper or tamper with the investigation in any manner;
(iii) That the petitioner shall not, directly or indirectly, make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer; and Kulendra Talukdar vs State Of Assam on 20 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/42103769/

